    "media:imagetext": "PAA\nPAN AMERICAN AI\nPA\nNY\nGENERAL OFFICE\nALAMEDA - CALIFORNIA\nDISTRICT TRAFFIC OFFICE\nMANILA HOTEL\nMANILA, P. I.\nbased upon an investment by us (without s-43) of roughly $ 550,000.\n6. Replacement of CNAC assets by the Govt to a\npoint approximately the same either in cash or equipment as enjoyed by the\ncompany on July 31st 1937. Another requiremenyt might be an increase\nin capital through waiver\nby both the American partners and the Ministry\nof rights to subscribe additional stock\nChinese private party might be willing torticipate and the take to third\nThis scheme would of course contemplate the\nresumption of negotiations with I,V, Soong and his group. aft the warn our.\nIt is realized that this program is almost a forlorn hope\nand may be quite impossible of accomplishment but if you are at all interested\nwe shall be glad to see what can be done\nThe M.D. is especially anxious\nto get me to come to Nanking for a discussion with the Ministry of Com.\ntold him that such a program must be based on a reestablishment of the good\nfaith which formerly characteized our relations and that step No.l would be\nthe strict carrying out of the deal which we made regarding payment of the\n$ 100,000 for the release of the DC-2\nHe promised that this payment\nwould be made the moment the DC-2 arrived at Hankow. and he in turn was\nassurerd that such a payment would constitute evidence of reconciliation\nThe M.D. claims that eevenue for the month of September\nwas over $ 135,000 and that it should be possible to build CNAC back up\npassenger\nI can procede to Hankow without any real danger and then go\nfrom there to Nanking on a British boat for a conference with Nelson Johnson\nand the Ministry of Communications.\nThe prospects Bf working out something\nconstructive, no matter how improbable of accomplishment would seem to\nwarrant the expense of such a trip and I am entirely willing to go as the\nrisk is very small.\nplike to\nThe M.D. would like to buy both Commodores and operate them\nwith the Dolphin between Ichang and Nanking. From Ichang he would operate\nbe flown by Harry Smith,\nSweet (both of whom are now flying for CNAE)\nand one other pilot\nBond would act as Operations\nManager and he wold\nhave to be assurred of a free hand in the management.\nWilke and Larsen, both\nold timers with the ground\nend of CNAC would rejoin the company.\nBond, Lum and Wong all left this morning in the DC-2 with\nHarry Smith for Hankow,\nBond and the M D may go on to Nanking for a prelim-\ninary talk with the M of C regarding the basis of our re-association •\nAs previously stated this program is a bit visionary but it promises\ntangible immediate and prospective returns on Paa investment than any\nclaim that we might eventually establish against an unfriendly and con-\ntentious Chinese Government.\nThis letter is written on a strange machine in our traffic\nwhile a party of drunks fifty feet away are making merry to the\nmusic of the Filipino orchestra of the Hotel. Please do me the favor of\nabsorbing as much of it as may be at all intelligible and then without\nshowing it to anyone\nelse burn it up.\nnanks\nPAN AMERICAN AIRWAYS\nEM - GENERAL\nOFFICES -195 E. 42\nYORK\nCITY\nD.S. Taxas Co was paid and releass Completed Oct. 54",
